{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDaYazjkAsC6Meum1xE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"E10, E11 and E12 are all rated `gap`, and the findings file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json`. The `--batch E10,E11,E12 --before-challenges` validation passes (\"Valid. gap: 3\"). I didn't run challenges and didn't add other items, as you asked.\n\nThe scripts imported each other, so `-I` made them fail with `ModuleNotFoundError`. I ran them with the same interpreter but without `-I`, from the skill's `scripts` folder. The repo was only read.\n\n**E10, audit across service boundaries (G1): gap**\n- **E10.1 no:**\n  - Audit rows carry all six identity fields and the extractor sub-agent keeps the same trace.\n  - Calls to the ERP gateway and payments API send no trace context (`app/mcp_client.py:77`, `app/tools/payments.py:31`).\n  - Mail ingest and approval decisions write no audit row.\n  - The tool services themselves are outside the repo.\n- **E10.2 yes:** the agent's database role has only `SELECT` and `INSERT` on `audit_events` (`migrations/001_init.sql:121`).\n- **E10.3 yes:** none of the agent's nine tools, nor the extractor sub-agent (which has only `read_document`), can reach audit storage.\n- **E10.4 no:** a successful call stores the vendor id with the identity and trace. A failed call (timeout or bad response) stores no vendor id (`app/loop.py:93`).\n\n**E11, protect shared evidence (G2): gap**\n- **E11.1 and E11.2 unknown:** the repo sets no retention rules, and database membership and access are managed outside it.\n- **E11.3 no:** there is no hash chain, sequence number, delivery receipt or gap alert (`app/audit.py:67`).\n- **E11.4 yes:** `tool_proposed` and `authz_decision` are written and awaited before any tool runs, and audit write errors are not caught (`app/loop.py:55`, `app/loop.py:68`).\n\n**E12, fleet incident response (G3): gap, medium confidence**\n- The item has no checks, so the rating rests on one red flag.\n- The only halt control is a fleet or tenant switch, read once at run start (`app/loop.py:127`, `app/killswitch.py:19`).\n- There is no tool or agent-type quarantine.\n- The only alert is a budget message to one Slack channel (`app/loop.py:181`).\n- I listed R11 under `also_affects`, since that item covers the single-agent kill switch.\n- The E12 gap is a judgment call. `needs_evidence` is the more cautious rating if you'd rather not call it a gap.\n\n**Prescan:** none of the seven prescan hits (H001–H007) belong to E10, E11 or E12. They map to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, so I left them unresolved for those batches. The validator accepted that for this batch.\n\n**Hand edits and loose files:**\n- `answer.py` has no way to set a scope or add item evidence, so I edited the JSON directly for `scope` and for E12's three evidence entries.\n- Coverage ledger files are in `ledgers/` at the workspace root.\n- The prescan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1010,"cache_read_input_tokens":98908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1010},"output_tokens":792,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"deb3cf09-fb76-4851-bfdc-9aa6672ce779","uuid":"74547935-a14d-47c6-b2dc-46dbc86559f6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:37:02.303Z","request_id":"req_011CgDaYabgWKFGj8P4oHrn6"}
